<h3>Step 2: Creative Localization (Complete 1 Week Before Launch)</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Copy Translation:</strong> Native proofreading + cultural sensitivity review</li>
<li><strong>Visual Adaptation:</strong> Color saturation adjustment, model face replacement</li>
<li><strong>Landing Page:</strong> Payment method integration, privacy policy page, language toggle</li>
<li><strong>Compliance Check:</strong> Religious/political sensitive word filter, copyright confirmation</li>
</ol>
<h3>Step 3: Test Launch (Phased Budget)</h3>
<ol>
<li>Start with $50/day for 3 days</li>
<li>If CTR &gt; 2%, scale up. If CTR &lt; 1%, revise creatives</li>
<li>Replicate high-performing creatives across other language regions</li>
</ol>
<h3>Step 4: Weekly Data Review</h3>
<ul>
<li>Compare CPM, CPC, and CTR across language regions</li>
<li>Document cultural feedback on creatives</li>
<li>Update your "Localization FAQ Database"</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Summary</h2>
<p>Southeast Asia and LatAm each have unique characteristics, but the core principle is the same: <strong>Make local users feel like "this ad understands me."</strong></p>
